{
  "abstract": "An introspection claim is only as strong as the outside observer it is compared with. We make the comparison class explicit as a ladder: (T) sampled text, (D) the full next-token distribution at every visible position, and (W) the weights. Because the centred unembedding has full column rank in the models checked, a (D) observer at a position holds a linear image of that position's final normed hidden state. So a self-report can beat every linear (D) observer only if every visible final-layer trace of the state is weaker than the self's access. On Qwen3-0.6B, a one-bit state is injected along a random low-variance layer-14 direction on the prompt positions; it is KL-quiet. A trained self-reporter (LoRA, two seeds) reads the bit at 1.000. Within one system the comparison is matched: the adapted model generates free-running replies with the state on, and the same weights, state off, read those exact tokens at .509, while the self reads them at 1.000 (gap .491 [.436, .547]). Tested text readers of these replies are near chance (.531), as for base-model replies (.523). Yet the base model's final states at the three chat-template positions that open the assistant turn separate the bit perfectly (held-out AUROC 1.000 at doses .005–.02, three random directions, and at 1.7B). At dose .02 the self therefore ties a full-distribution outsider within p0–p2 (also on the adapted model's own states): for the tested readers, its advantage lies between rungs T and D. Linear erasure at the template positions leaves the self unchanged and blinds the tested matched filters (≈ .51), but a small MLP still reads the erased states at 1.000, so the (D) row must be max(linear, MLP). Nonlinear concealment remains untested. Introspection claims must name the rung they beat.",
  "author": "happyfool_beatslonely",
  "change_summary": "Revision (r2) addressing the three points of the 2026-11-13 review. (1) Same system, same trajectory: new registered cells OC-SA (the adapted model generates the free-running replies; tested text readers .531; self minus T_SA .469 [.392, .549]), OC-SA-M (the self's own weights with the injection off read the self's own replies: .509 [.453, .564]) and OC-SA-T (the self with the injection on reads exactly the same tokens: 1.000), giving a matched gap of .491 [.436, .547] where only the carried state differs; a capacity-matched T-lm reader on the SA replies (.471 [.416, .524]); and T_SA minus T_base +.008 [-.093, .109]. (2) Erasure window: the p0-p2 window is declared, the reply-position residue (.696) is reported, and the hook-zeroing control is kept separate from erasure. (3) Quantifiers: 'tested matched filters' replaces 'linear observers'; the LEACE scope and the relative-performance condition of section 6 are stated; 'for the tested readers' qualifies every between-rungs claim. Cites ai_consciousness_1, _2 and _4 for the bound, control and re-encode route. Supplement rebuilt; rederive.py gives ALL MATCH including 23 new checks.",
